.DS_Store
node_modules/
*.log
.env*
dist/
build/

# THE ONE COMMITTED BUILD OUTPUT, AND IT IS MECHANISED RATHER THAN HONOURED (3F-2810). A composite
# action under .github/actions/ is checked out into the CALLER's workspace, so the only directory
# its step can rely on is its own: ${{ github.action_path }}. The file that step runs therefore
# travels with the action, which means a build output in the diff — the exact thing the rule above
# exists to stop, carved out at exactly these paths and nowhere wider.
#
# THE DIRECTORY LINE COMES FIRST AND IS LOAD-BEARING: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so re-including only the .mjs would re-include nothing at all and the
# bundles would silently never be committed.
#
# What stops the carve-out rotting is lint:action-bundles, which rebuilds each of these from its
# source and reds on any difference (@SCN-ACT-003, cited over the real tree by @SCN-ACT-004).
!.github/actions/*/dist/
!.github/actions/*/dist/*.mjs

.claude/*.local.json

# Reconciliation run output is NOT tracked in the repo. A report enumerates a
# codebase's gaps, dangling anchors, and watermelons — more sensitive than the
# code itself — so stored runs live OUTSIDE the repo. Ignore the whole runs/ tree
# with NO re-includes, so no new in-repo run path can ever be committed by
# accident. The lint:no-committed-reports CI guard enforces this over the real tree.
runs/**

# Mutation-testing output. `.stryker-tmp/` is the sandbox Stryker copies the tree
# into per run; `reports/` holds the HTML/JSON mutation report, which enumerates
# which domain lines no test kills — the same sensitivity class as a
# reconciliation report, so it is never tracked either.
.stryker-tmp/
reports/

# Operator-local working notes — never committed (swept into a slice PR by `git add -A`, 3F-2690).
CLAUDE.local.md
